{#- A retired address (the become wave, 2026-10-06: /roadmaps/ became /become/,
    and the Russian mirror was withdrawn). GitHub Pages sends no HTTP redirects,
    so the old URL keeps a page that sends the reader on: a meta refresh for
    browsers, a canonical for crawlers pointing at where the content lives now,
    noindex so the stub itself never ranks, and a plain link for any browser
    that refuses to refresh. scripts/check-build.mjs proves every stub lands on a
    page the build produced. #}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Moved — {{ site.name }}</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}{{ redirectTo }}">
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ redirectTo }}">
</head>
<body>
  <p>This page has moved: <a href="{{ redirectTo }}">{{ site.url }}{{ redirectTo }}</a></p>
</body>
</html>
